From e1182dc58521a7b29dba64c239e6c175d8659d24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: faycal <faycalelhandi9@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:17:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/26] perf(libc): write alarms on resident guest pages
 instead of polling GetWriteWatch

APS5_WRITE_ALARMS=1: when WindowsMappings::Collect walks a resident run, the writable pages in the
range are made read-only first ("armed", per view and in a per-run bitmap), then GetWriteWatch resets
as before. A later collect of a range whose pages are all still armed returns at once: nothing can
have been written. The first CPU write to an armed page faults once; HandleWrite restores the page's
protection, clears its bits and lets the write proceed, so the write watch reports it next time.
BeginHostWrite (host writes and imports), Pin and SetProtection disarm the pages they touch.

The game writes ~80 pages per frame while the driver collected ~1300 ranges per frame. Astro Bot world
map: 3.9M collects skipped, ~19k alarm faults per 10 s; collect time 16.7 -> 9.8 s per run; committer
cost 39.9 -> 31.6 us per commit; presents 111-114 (steady earlier runs) -> 118-119 per 10 s, GPU idle
gaps -> ~21 ms per frame. Screenshots correct. Also counts the written pages collects find.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
